                  {
                    "value": "Insight 1: Retention is extremely low - in every monthly cohort fewer than 1% of new customers buy again in the next month (e.g. Nov-2017: 7,059 new customers, only 40 returned in month 1 = 0.6%).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#33475B"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Insight 2: Only 2,015 customers (2.2%) ever returned on a different day. 'Repeat by orders' (3.0%) overstates loyalty, because ~786 customers placed two orders on the same day.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#33475B"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Insight 3: Retention did not improve as the store grew, so growth came only from acquiring new customers - retention is the main untapped growth lever.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#33475B"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
